{#
compose/_undo_too_late.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The cancel arrived after SendMessageHandler had already claimed the message.

This template exists because the alternative was lying. Every undo used to
answer with the dock-undo stream — "send cancelled", window restored — whether
or not the cancel had actually taken, and a cancel clicked in the last fraction
of the hold does not take. The user was told the one thing that was not true
about the one action that cannot be reversed.

So: an ERROR toast, not an info one, because something the user asked for did
not happen; and no window, because there is no draft to reopen. Restoring the
composer here would put an editable copy of an already-sent mail on screen, and
the next autosave would file it as a draft standing beside the sent copy.

And the page is left exactly as a send that ran its course leaves it, by
including the very same partial: whatever window this cancel came from is
describing a message that has gone, so it closes, and the message takes its
place in the conversation. That used to be a bare "empty the dock", which was
right only because the inline composer had already been replaced by a
countdown bar before this could be reached. It is not any more — the window is
still open, still holding a copy of a mail that is on the wire — so saying
"too late" without also closing it would leave the user an editable draft of
something already sent.

Variables: message, thread (MessageThread|null), ctx
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type: 'error',
            message: 'toast.send_too_late'|trans,
            extra: { hide_after: 8000 },
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

{# The error above IS this send's notification. Nothing has to be suppressed
   any more: _sent.stream stopped claiming success, because at the moment it
   runs nobody knows whether the send worked. #}
{% include 'compose/_sent.stream.html.twig' with {
    message: message,
    thread:  thread,
    ctx:     ctx,
} only %}
